I open the door.
It is wonderfully warm inside.
The air smells of fresh coffee.
The café is very busy today.
Almost all tables are taken.
I look around.
I spot an empty table.
It stands right by a large window.
I walk quickly to the table.
An older woman sits at the next table.
I ask her politely: "Excuse me, is this table still free?"
The woman nods and says: "Yes, of course."
I smile and answer: "Thank you very much!"
Then I take off my green winter coat.
I put the coat on the wooden chair.
This way I save my spot.
But I keep my backpack safely on my shoulder.
My laptop is in there, after all.
Now I go to the counter.
